    "message": "feat(tools): add dogfood.py, move the docs output to docs-site/dist, prune .gitignore (#3035)\n\n- tools/dogfood.py sets up BMad in a fresh checkout or worktree with no\n  inference: it installs a subset of skills with npx skills (from the\n  checkout itself by default), builds _bmad with the bmad skill's\n  setup.py, and copies core.output_folder from the main checkout's local\n  config. Options: --source, --skills, --agents, --custom-from, --reset,\n  and an optional dogfood.toml. It exits non-zero when setup reports\n  problems or unmet requirements.\n- The docs site builds to Astro's default docs-site/dist instead of the\n  repo-root build/site, so it no longer shares a name with docs/build/.\n  The Pages upload path, build script, validators, test, and README\n  follow.\n- .gitignore drops rules for things nothing creates any more, makes\n  .agents and .ai match as directories, restores .gemini, adds .idea/\n  and /dogfood.toml, and folds the rest into two sections."
  },
